        "id": 142847,
        "name": "Arcanist Lupus",
        "username": "Arcanist_Lupus",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arcanist_lupus/{size}/2169_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-06-18T06:17:30.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I agree with you, but we don't have much choice in the matter. &nbsp;As far as I understand it's a matter of timing. &nbsp;Bills are chosen for redesign based on a number of factors, and the personality of the representative face is not one of them. &nbsp;So it's either the ten now, or the twenty in another decade or so.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I do find it rather darkly amusing that the first bill to have a woman's face will be the ten which is probably the least used of the smaller bills (excepting, of course, the two).</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Maybe we can have Hamilton bump off Jackson for the twenty when it comes up for redesign?</p>",
